The mesh keeps the source's native frame -- x = the ~99 mm long bar the lenses are arrayed across,
y = height ~23 mm, z = depth ~20 mm with +z the lens face's outward normal -- the same convention as
the d435 and d455 meshes, so no reorientation was applied.

The `d415_color` camera pose baked into roqsim_sensors/models/d415/d415.xml is placed on the front lens
face in that mesh-local frame; its `fovy` is the D415 colour vertical FOV from the datasheet, not a
value measured off the mesh.
